# PROTOTYPE — injection template, runs INSIDE the living target instance (clone-and-run).
# Resolves an expression to the static $fullname of its method.
# Omnis uses DIFFERENT notation to CALL a method vs. to REFERENCE it as an object, so the
# expression is evaluated in the live instance and the method object is reached from there:
#   - method inside an $obj (any nesting): reachable via [pExpr].$obj().$methods
#   - plain class method:                  reachable via [pExpr].$class().$methods
# Returns the static $fullname (string), transportable across the instance boundary;
# the caller resolves it with [fullname].$ref.
# Note: evaluating [pExpr] EXECUTES the intermediate '()' links of the reference chain to reach
# the method object — a link with side effects would fire here.

If not([pExpr].$cando) ## expression cannot be evaluated in this instance
	Quit method ''
End If

If [pExpr].$obj().$class ## method sits in an $obj on the window
	Quit method [pExpr].$obj().$methods.$findname([pExpr].$name).$fullname
Else ## plain class method
	Quit method [pExpr].$class().$methods.$findname([pExpr].$name).$fullname
End If